  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, IVRCSDKPreprocessAvatarCallback callbacks can make changes that result in final avatars that would normally fail the VRCSDK's hard limits. For instance, if parameters are added to the parameters file, it's possible for >256 bits to be used on accident, breaking the parameters entirely in game.\n\nCurrently, we are forced to reimplement these checks piecemeal, but it would be nice if the VRCSDK would re-verify its own limits after all IVRCSDKPreprocessAvatarCallbacks have been invoked.\n\n(giving some feedback about final performance rank would also be nice, but that one's a more difficult problem to solve, as IVRCSDKPreprocessAvatarCallbacks are often quite slow)",
